{"parentUuid":"60d3212f-e892-4087-bf1a-67e95ef6564e","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"5d3cc83e-4643-4c1b-a0f8-8286c23c1c00","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"swift-chasing-cookie","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01ThDrZRMwnUaghUZ1mBjgWA","type":"tool_result","content":"# ClusterData 2011 Traces Overview\n\nThis dataset documents a month-long snapshot of Google's Borg cluster management system from May 2011, capturing operations across approximately 12,500 machines.\n\n## Key Details\n\n**Timeline & Scale:** The trace begins at 7 PM EDT on May 1, 2011, and spans 29 days of datacenter activity.\n\n**Data Format:** The information follows the v2.1 schema with a unique addition—\"a randomly-picked 1 second sample of CPU usage from within the associated 5-minute usage-reporting period.\" This enables researchers to model task utilization patterns statistically.\n\n**Accessibility:** The complete compressed dataset occupies roughly 41GB and resides in Google Storage, downloadable via the gsutil tool.\n\n## Notable Limitations\n\nThe dataset has several documented quirks worth considering:\n\n- Disk metrics are incomplete, covering only the initial two weeks due to monitoring infrastructure changes\n- A negligible fraction of jobs (approximately 70 instances) lack associated task records despite having scheduling events\n- Minor data quality issues affect approximately 0.013% of task events and 0.0008% of job events\n- Certain performance metrics (CPI and MAI) contain measurement artifacts, necessitating filtering for meaningful analysis\n\n## Access & Licensing\n\nThe trace is available under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 license, requiring attribution for use. Researchers should join the project's mailing list and refer to the complete schema documentation before downloading."}]},"uuid":"35f03916-5691-4c55-b454-7031d2da4b1d","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:46:50.179Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":4137,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# ClusterData 2011 Traces Overview\n\nThis dataset documents a month-long snapshot of Google's Borg cluster management system from May 2011, capturing operations across approximately 12,500 machines.\n\n## Key Details\n\n**Timeline & Scale:** The trace begins at 7 PM EDT on May 1, 2011, and spans 29 days of datacenter activity.\n\n**Data Format:** The information follows the v2.1 schema with a unique addition—\"a randomly-picked 1 second sample of CPU usage from within the associated 5-minute usage-reporting period.\" This enables researchers to model task utilization patterns statistically.\n\n**Accessibility:** The complete compressed dataset occupies roughly 41GB and resides in Google Storage, downloadable via the gsutil tool.\n\n## Notable Limitations\n\nThe dataset has several documented quirks worth considering:\n\n- Disk metrics are incomplete, covering only the initial two weeks due to monitoring infrastructure changes\n- A negligible fraction of jobs (approximately 70 instances) lack associated task records despite having scheduling events\n- Minor data quality issues affect approximately 0.013% of task events and 0.0008% of job events\n- Certain performance metrics (CPI and MAI) contain measurement artifacts, necessitating filtering for meaningful analysis\n\n## Access & Licensing\n\nThe trace is available under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 license, requiring attribution for use. Researchers should join the project's mailing list and refer to the complete schema documentation before downloading.","durationMs":5388,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/cluster-data/master/ClusterData2011_2.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"60d3212f-e892-4087-bf1a-67e95ef6564e"}
