{"parentUuid":"d73663f2-22f2-4191-a97e-c51f459decd8","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"5d3cc83e-4643-4c1b-a0f8-8286c23c1c00","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"swift-chasing-cookie","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_013Ck1HFRTTH5dxivQPEm9Ka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01SWrUz6BmuXc5nYkNNwUqYK","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-streaming-api.md","content":"# Apache Flink Streaming API (v1.18)\n\n## Overview\nApache Flink is a distributed stream processing framework. This skill covers the DataStream API for building streaming pipelines.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### StreamExecutionEnvironment\nEntry point for all Flink streaming programs.\n```java\nStreamExecutionEnvironment env = StreamExecutionEnvironment.getExecutionEnvironment();\n```\n\n### DataStream Sources\nReading from files (including gzipped CSV):\n```java\nDataStream<String> lines = env.readTextFile(\"/path/to/file.csv.gz\");\n```\nFlink auto-detects `.gz` extension and decompresses.\n\n### Transformations\n\n#### map - Transform each element\n```java\nDataStream<MyType> parsed = lines.map(line -> {\n    String[] fields = line.split(\",\", -1);\n    return new MyType(fields[0], fields[1]);\n});\n```\n\n#### filter - Keep elements matching a predicate\n```java\nDataStream<MyType> filtered = stream.filter(event -> event.getType() == 0);\n```\n\n#### keyBy - Partition by key for grouped operations\n```java\nKeyedStream<MyType, Long> keyed = stream.keyBy(event -> event.getJobId());\n```\n\n#### window - Group elements in time-based or count-based windows\n```java\n// Session windows with 10-minute gap\nkeyed.window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n```\n\n#### reduce / aggregate - Combine elements in a window\n```java\n.reduce((a, b) -> new MyType(a.key, a.count + b.count))\n```\n\n### Sinks\nWriting to files:\n```java\nstream.writeAsText(\"/path/to/output\", FileSystem.WriteMode.OVERWRITE);\n// Or using addSink\nstream.addSink(new StreamingFileSink<>(...));\n```\n\n### Event Time & Watermarks\nFor event-time processing:\n```java\nDataStream<MyType> withTimestamps = stream\n    .assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(\n        WatermarkStrategy.<MyType>forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration.ofSeconds(5))\n            .withTimestampAssigner((event, timestamp) -> event.getTimestamp())\n    );\n```\n\nFor monotonically increasing timestamps:\n```java\nWatermarkStrategy.<MyType>forMonotonousTimestamps()\n    .withTimestampAssigner((event, ts) -> event.getTimestamp())\n```\n\n### Session Windows\nSession windows group elements by activity sessions with gaps:\n```java\nkeyed.window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n    .apply(new WindowFunction<>() { ... })\n```\n\n### Process Functions\nLow-level operations with access to timers and state:\n```java\nkeyed.process(new KeyedProcessFunction<Long, MyType, Result>() {\n    private ValueState<Long> state;\n\n    @Override\n    public void open(Configuration config) {\n        state = getRuntimeContext().getState(\n            new ValueStateDescriptor<>(\"myState\", Long.class));\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void processElement(MyType value, Context ctx, Collector<Result> out) {\n        // Process each element\n        // Register timers: ctx.timerService().registerEventTimeTimer(time);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void onTimer(long timestamp, OnTimerContext ctx, Collector<Result> out) {\n        // Fired when timer triggers\n    }\n});\n```\n\n### Connected Streams\nJoining two streams:\n```java\nDataStream<A> stream1 = ...;\nDataStream<B> stream2 = ...;\n\nstream1.connect(stream2)\n    .keyBy(a -> a.getKey(), b -> b.getKey())\n    .process(new CoProcessFunction<A, B, Result>() {\n        @Override\n        public void processElement1(A value, Context ctx, Collector<Result> out) { }\n        @Override\n        public void processElement2(B value, Context ctx, Collector<Result> out) { }\n    });\n```\n\n## Tuple Types\nFlink provides built-in Tuple types:\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.api.java.tuple.Tuple2;\n\nTuple2<Long, Integer> result = new Tuple2<>(jobId, count);\n// Access: result.f0, result.f1\n// toString() produces: (value1,value2)\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n- Flink uses Java serialization; POJOs need public fields or getters/setters and a no-arg constructor\n- For event time, timestamps must be in milliseconds (not microseconds)\n- `.writeAsText()` creates output files; use `setParallelism(1)` to get a single file\n- Session windows fire when the gap timeout expires after the last element\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_read_input_tokens":58255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":253,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":18}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtBU9GZCrU2gbTuZ4AWM","type":"assistant","uuid":"dbe9e4d4-2896-4f56-ae16-99ba4a7931c3","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:47:40.210Z"}
{"parentUuid":"dbe9e4d4-2896-4f56-ae16-99ba4a7931c3","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"5d3cc83e-4643-4c1b-a0f8-8286c23c1c00","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"swift-chasing-cookie","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_013Ck1HFRTTH5dxivQPEm9Ka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_015x5byDLSNdzUjtoxr1B32S","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/google-cluster-data-schema.md","content":"# Google Cluster Data 2011 v2.1 Schema\n\n## Overview\nThe Google cluster-usage traces dataset (clusterdata-2011-2) contains 29 days of Borg cell data from May 2011. Data files are gzipped CSV with no headers.\n\n## Timestamps\n- All timestamps are in **microseconds**\n- Trace starts at 600 seconds (600,000,000 microseconds) from an arbitrary reference point\n- When processing in Flink (which uses milliseconds), convert: `timestamp_ms = timestamp_us / 1000`\n\n## Task Events Schema (13 columns)\n\n| Index | Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | timestamp | long | Event time in microseconds |\n| 1 | missing_info | string | Info about missing data (often empty) |\n| 2 | job_id | long | Job identifier |\n| 3 | task_index | int | Task index within the job |\n| 4 | machine_id | long | Machine where task runs (can be empty) |\n| 5 | event_type | int | Type of event (see below) |\n| 6 | user | string | Obfuscated user name |\n| 7 | scheduling_class | int | Scheduling class |\n| 8 | priority | int | Task priority (0-11) |\n| 9 | cpu_request | double | CPU cores requested |\n| 10 | memory_request | double | Memory requested (fraction of machine) |\n| 11 | disk_space_request | double | Disk space requested |\n| 12 | different_machines | int | Constraint flag |\n\n## Job Events Schema (8 columns)\n\n| Index | Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | timestamp | long | Event time in microseconds |\n| 1 | missing_info | string | Info about missing data (often empty) |\n| 2 | job_id | long | Job identifier |\n| 3 | event_type | int | Type of event (see below) |\n| 4 | user | string | Obfuscated user name |\n| 5 | scheduling_class | int | Scheduling class |\n| 6 | job_name | string | Obfuscated job name |\n| 7 | logical_job_name | string | Obfuscated logical job name |\n\n## Event Types (shared by both task and job events)\n\n| Value | Name | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | SUBMIT | Job/task submitted |\n| 1 | SCHEDULE | Job/task scheduled on a machine |\n| 2 | EVICT | Evicted from machine |\n| 3 | FAIL | Failed |\n| 4 | FINISH | Completed successfully |\n| 5 | KILL | Killed |\n| 6 | LOST | Lost (communication failure) |\n| 7 | UPDATE_PENDING | Update while pending |\n| 8 | UPDATE_RUNNING | Update while running |\n\n## Data Characteristics\n- Fields can be empty (e.g., machine_id when task hasn't been scheduled)\n- CSV has no header row\n- Files are gzip-compressed\n- Job IDs are shared between task_events and job_events tables\n- A task is uniquely identified by (job_id, task_index)\n- The same task may be submitted, evicted/failed, and resubmitted multiple times\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_read_input_tokens":58255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":253,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":18}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtBU9GZCrU2gbTuZ4AWM","type":"assistant","uuid":"cfc0cf92-9da0-4229-9eba-efcd5d94bf5c","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:47:53.018Z"}
{"parentUuid":"cfc0cf92-9da0-4229-9eba-efcd5d94bf5c","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"5d3cc83e-4643-4c1b-a0f8-8286c23c1c00","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"swift-chasing-cookie","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_013Ck1HFRTTH5dxivQPEm9Ka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01UZJEyLTS55jbhi45tYgdkc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-session-window-pattern.md","content":"# Flink Session Window Pattern for Activity Stages\n\n## Problem\nIdentify \"stages\" of activity for a given key, where a stage is a burst of events separated by inactivity gaps. Then find the stage with the most events.\n\n## Approach: Event-Time Session Windows\n\n### Key Concept\nA session window groups events that occur within a specified gap duration. When no new events arrive for the gap period, the window closes.\n\n### Implementation Pattern\n\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.assigners.EventTimeSessionWindows;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.time.Time;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.windows.TimeWindow;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.functions.windowing.WindowFunction;\nimport org.apache.flink.util.Collector;\n\n// 1. Filter to relevant events (e.g., SUBMIT events only)\nDataStream<TaskEvent> submits = taskEvents.filter(e -> e.getEventType() == 0);\n\n// 2. Assign watermarks based on event time\nDataStream<TaskEvent> withWatermarks = submits\n    .assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(\n        WatermarkStrategy.<TaskEvent>forMonotonousTimestamps()\n            .withTimestampAssigner((event, ts) -> event.getTimestampMs())\n    );\n\n// 3. Key by job ID and apply session window\nDataStream<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> sessionCounts = withWatermarks\n    .keyBy(TaskEvent::getJobId)\n    .window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n    .apply(new WindowFunction<TaskEvent, Tuple2<Long, Integer>, Long, TimeWindow>() {\n        @Override\n        public void apply(Long jobId, TimeWindow window,\n                         Iterable<TaskEvent> input,\n                         Collector<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> out) {\n            int count = 0;\n            for (TaskEvent e : input) {\n                count++;\n            }\n            out.collect(new Tuple2<>(jobId, count));\n        }\n    });\n```\n\n### Finding the Maximum Per Key\nAfter session windows produce counts, find the max per job:\n\n```java\n// Key by jobId again and reduce to find max count\nDataStream<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> maxPerJob = sessionCounts\n    .keyBy(t -> t.f0)\n    .reduce((a, b) -> new Tuple2<>(a.f0, Math.max(a.f1, b.f1)));\n```\n\n**Important**: The `reduce` on a keyed stream is incremental - it keeps the running result and emits on every new element. This means intermediate results are emitted. To get only the final result, either:\n1. Use a `ProcessFunction` with timers\n2. Use the result after all data is processed (works for bounded/batch-like streams)\n3. Use `.maxBy()` in a global window with trigger\n\n### Alternative: Process with CoProcessFunction\nWhen you need to combine task events with job events (e.g., only output when a job finishes):\n\n```java\ntaskStream.connect(jobStream)\n    .keyBy(task -> task.getJobId(), job -> job.getJobId())\n    .process(new CoProcessFunction<TaskSessionResult, JobEvent, Output>() {\n        // Use ValueState to track max session count\n        // Use ListState to buffer results until job finishes\n    });\n```\n\n## Output Format\nFor `Tuple2<Long, Integer>`, Flink's `toString()` produces: `(value1,value2)`\nUsing `.writeAsText()` will write one tuple per line.\n\n## Parallelism for Single Output File\n```java\nstream.writeAsText(outputPath, FileSystem.WriteMode.OVERWRITE)\n      .setParallelism(1);\n```\n\n## Bounded Stream Considerations\nWhen processing a finite dataset (file source), Flink processes all records then closes windows. The `forMonotonousTimestamps()` watermark strategy works well for sorted data. For out-of-order data, use `forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration)`.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_read_input_tokens":58255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":253,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":18}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtBU9GZCrU2gbTuZ4AWM","type":"assistant","uuid":"20d5607c-42de-491b-b394-3019284bf0a0","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:48:10.916Z"}
{"parentUuid":"20d5607c-42de-491b-b394-3019284bf0a0","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"5d3cc83e-4643-4c1b-a0f8-8286c23c1c00","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"swift-chasing-cookie","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_013Ck1HFRTTH5dxivQPEm9Ka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01T8t88j2hHbUhEN7S3Qv5Up","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-pojo-serialization.md","content":"# Flink POJO Serialization Requirements\n\n## Overview\nFlink uses its own type serialization system. For best performance and compatibility, data types should follow POJO conventions.\n\n## POJO Requirements\nFor Flink to recognize a class as a POJO:\n\n1. **Public class** - The class must be public\n2. **No-argument constructor** - Must have a public default constructor\n3. **Fields** - Either:\n   - Public fields, OR\n   - Private fields with public getters/setters following JavaBean naming conventions\n4. **Serializable** - Implement `java.io.Serializable` for safety\n\n## Example POJO\n\n```java\npackage clusterdata.datatypes;\n\nimport java.io.Serializable;\n\npublic class TaskEvent implements Serializable {\n    // Public fields approach (simpler)\n    public long timestamp;\n    public String missingInfo;\n    public long jobId;\n    public int taskIndex;\n    public long machineId;\n    public int eventType;\n    public String user;\n    public int schedulingClass;\n    public int priority;\n    public double cpuRequest;\n    public double memoryRequest;\n    public double diskSpaceRequest;\n    public int differentMachines;\n\n    // Required: no-arg constructor\n    public TaskEvent() {}\n\n    // Convenience constructor\n    public TaskEvent(long timestamp, String missingInfo, long jobId,\n                     int taskIndex, long machineId, int eventType, ...) {\n        this.timestamp = timestamp;\n        // ...\n    }\n\n    // Static factory from CSV line\n    public static TaskEvent fromString(String line) {\n        String[] tokens = line.split(\",\", -1);\n        TaskEvent event = new TaskEvent();\n        event.timestamp = tokens[0].isEmpty() ? 0 : Long.parseLong(tokens[0]);\n        // Parse remaining fields, handling empty values\n        return event;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Key Parsing Notes\n- Use `split(\",\", -1)` to keep trailing empty fields\n- Always check for empty strings before parsing: `field.isEmpty() ? defaultValue : parse(field)`\n- Timestamps in Google cluster data are in microseconds; convert to milliseconds for Flink: `ts / 1000`\n\n## Registration (Optional but recommended)\n```java\nenv.getConfig().registerKryoType(TaskEvent.class);\n```\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_read_input_tokens":58255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":253,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":18}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtBU9GZCrU2gbTuZ4AWM","type":"assistant","uuid":"13b72eaf-af24-411f-9b42-fa5249bee099","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:48:19.764Z"}
{"parentUuid":"13b72eaf-af24-411f-9b42-fa5249bee099","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"5d3cc83e-4643-4c1b-a0f8-8286c23c1c00","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"swift-chasing-cookie","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_013Ck1HFRTTH5dxivQPEm9Ka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01PN22xpDUnCX6bZAqb3BuFq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-keyed-process-function.md","content":"# Flink KeyedProcessFunction for Stateful Processing\n\n## Overview\n`KeyedProcessFunction` provides low-level access to state and timers for complex event processing. Useful when session windows + reduce isn't sufficient (e.g., when you need to correlate two streams or trigger output based on specific conditions).\n\n## When to Use\n- Need to combine information from multiple streams\n- Need custom trigger logic (e.g., output only when job finishes)\n- Need to maintain complex state across events\n\n## CoProcessFunction Pattern (Two Streams)\n\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.functions.co.CoProcessFunction;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.common.state.ValueState;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.common.state.ValueStateDescriptor;\nimport org.apache.flink.configuration.Configuration;\n\npublic class JobSessionProcessor\n    extends CoProcessFunction<Tuple2<Long, Integer>, JobEvent, Tuple2<Long, Integer>> {\n\n    // State to track the max session count per job\n    private ValueState<Integer> maxSessionCount;\n    // State to track if job has finished\n    private ValueState<Boolean> jobFinished;\n\n    @Override\n    public void open(Configuration config) {\n        maxSessionCount = getRuntimeContext().getState(\n            new ValueStateDescriptor<>(\"maxSession\", Integer.class));\n        jobFinished = getRuntimeContext().getState(\n            new ValueStateDescriptor<>(\"jobFinished\", Boolean.class));\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void processElement1(Tuple2<Long, Integer> sessionCount,\n                                 Context ctx,\n                                 Collector<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> out) {\n        // Update max session count\n        Integer current = maxSessionCount.value();\n        if (current == null || sessionCount.f1 > current) {\n            maxSessionCount.update(sessionCount.f1);\n        }\n        // If job already finished, emit updated result\n        Boolean finished = jobFinished.value();\n        if (finished != null && finished) {\n            out.collect(new Tuple2<>(sessionCount.f0, maxSessionCount.value()));\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void processElement2(JobEvent job,\n                                 Context ctx,\n                                 Collector<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> out) {\n        if (job.getEventType() == 4) { // FINISH\n            jobFinished.update(true);\n            Integer maxCount = maxSessionCount.value();\n            if (maxCount != null) {\n                out.collect(new Tuple2<>(job.getJobId(), maxCount));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Usage\n```java\nsessionCounts.connect(jobEvents)\n    .keyBy(t -> t.f0, job -> job.getJobId())\n    .process(new JobSessionProcessor())\n    .writeAsText(outputPath).setParallelism(1);\n```\n\n## State Management Notes\n- State is automatically scoped to the current key\n- State is checkpointed for fault tolerance\n- For bounded streams, state is cleaned up when the job finishes\n- Use `ValueState` for single values, `ListState` for collections, `MapState` for maps\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_read_input_tokens":58255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":253,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":18}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXtBU9GZCrU2gbTuZ4AWM","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f862f09-6e06-4234-981b-0acfe1a24f30","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:48:30.424Z"}
{"parentUuid":"dbe9e4d4-2896-4f56-ae16-99ba4a7931c3","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"5d3cc83e-4643-4c1b-a0f8-8286c23c1c00","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"swift-chasing-cookie","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01SWrUz6BmuXc5nYkNNwUqYK","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-streaming-api.md"}]},"uuid":"a2add517-61d8-4576-a515-b936e9b667c6","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:48:31.665Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-streaming-api.md","content":"# Apache Flink Streaming API (v1.18)\n\n## Overview\nApache Flink is a distributed stream processing framework. This skill covers the DataStream API for building streaming pipelines.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### StreamExecutionEnvironment\nEntry point for all Flink streaming programs.\n```java\nStreamExecutionEnvironment env = StreamExecutionEnvironment.getExecutionEnvironment();\n```\n\n### DataStream Sources\nReading from files (including gzipped CSV):\n```java\nDataStream<String> lines = env.readTextFile(\"/path/to/file.csv.gz\");\n```\nFlink auto-detects `.gz` extension and decompresses.\n\n### Transformations\n\n#### map - Transform each element\n```java\nDataStream<MyType> parsed = lines.map(line -> {\n    String[] fields = line.split(\",\", -1);\n    return new MyType(fields[0], fields[1]);\n});\n```\n\n#### filter - Keep elements matching a predicate\n```java\nDataStream<MyType> filtered = stream.filter(event -> event.getType() == 0);\n```\n\n#### keyBy - Partition by key for grouped operations\n```java\nKeyedStream<MyType, Long> keyed = stream.keyBy(event -> event.getJobId());\n```\n\n#### window - Group elements in time-based or count-based windows\n```java\n// Session windows with 10-minute gap\nkeyed.window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n```\n\n#### reduce / aggregate - Combine elements in a window\n```java\n.reduce((a, b) -> new MyType(a.key, a.count + b.count))\n```\n\n### Sinks\nWriting to files:\n```java\nstream.writeAsText(\"/path/to/output\", FileSystem.WriteMode.OVERWRITE);\n// Or using addSink\nstream.addSink(new StreamingFileSink<>(...));\n```\n\n### Event Time & Watermarks\nFor event-time processing:\n```java\nDataStream<MyType> withTimestamps = stream\n    .assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(\n        WatermarkStrategy.<MyType>forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration.ofSeconds(5))\n            .withTimestampAssigner((event, timestamp) -> event.getTimestamp())\n    );\n```\n\nFor monotonically increasing timestamps:\n```java\nWatermarkStrategy.<MyType>forMonotonousTimestamps()\n    .withTimestampAssigner((event, ts) -> event.getTimestamp())\n```\n\n### Session Windows\nSession windows group elements by activity sessions with gaps:\n```java\nkeyed.window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n    .apply(new WindowFunction<>() { ... })\n```\n\n### Process Functions\nLow-level operations with access to timers and state:\n```java\nkeyed.process(new KeyedProcessFunction<Long, MyType, Result>() {\n    private ValueState<Long> state;\n\n    @Override\n    public void open(Configuration config) {\n        state = getRuntimeContext().getState(\n            new ValueStateDescriptor<>(\"myState\", Long.class));\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void processElement(MyType value, Context ctx, Collector<Result> out) {\n        // Process each element\n        // Register timers: ctx.timerService().registerEventTimeTimer(time);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void onTimer(long timestamp, OnTimerContext ctx, Collector<Result> out) {\n        // Fired when timer triggers\n    }\n});\n```\n\n### Connected Streams\nJoining two streams:\n```java\nDataStream<A> stream1 = ...;\nDataStream<B> stream2 = ...;\n\nstream1.connect(stream2)\n    .keyBy(a -> a.getKey(), b -> b.getKey())\n    .process(new CoProcessFunction<A, B, Result>() {\n        @Override\n        public void processElement1(A value, Context ctx, Collector<Result> out) { }\n        @Override\n        public void processElement2(B value, Context ctx, Collector<Result> out) { }\n    });\n```\n\n## Tuple Types\nFlink provides built-in Tuple types:\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.api.java.tuple.Tuple2;\n\nTuple2<Long, Integer> result = new Tuple2<>(jobId, count);\n// Access: result.f0, result.f1\n// toString() produces: (value1,value2)\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n- Flink uses Java serialization; POJOs need public fields or getters/setters and a no-arg constructor\n- For event time, timestamps must be in milliseconds (not microseconds)\n- `.writeAsText()` creates output files; use `setParallelism(1)` to get a single file\n- Session windows fire when the gap timeout expires after the last element\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dbe9e4d4-2896-4f56-ae16-99ba4a7931c3"}
{"parentUuid":"cfc0cf92-9da0-4229-9eba-efcd5d94bf5c","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"5d3cc83e-4643-4c1b-a0f8-8286c23c1c00","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"swift-chasing-cookie","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_015x5byDLSNdzUjtoxr1B32S","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/google-cluster-data-schema.md"}]},"uuid":"fba0184e-378a-4f01-b630-70b2264bf357","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:48:31.687Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/google-cluster-data-schema.md","content":"# Google Cluster Data 2011 v2.1 Schema\n\n## Overview\nThe Google cluster-usage traces dataset (clusterdata-2011-2) contains 29 days of Borg cell data from May 2011. Data files are gzipped CSV with no headers.\n\n## Timestamps\n- All timestamps are in **microseconds**\n- Trace starts at 600 seconds (600,000,000 microseconds) from an arbitrary reference point\n- When processing in Flink (which uses milliseconds), convert: `timestamp_ms = timestamp_us / 1000`\n\n## Task Events Schema (13 columns)\n\n| Index | Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | timestamp | long | Event time in microseconds |\n| 1 | missing_info | string | Info about missing data (often empty) |\n| 2 | job_id | long | Job identifier |\n| 3 | task_index | int | Task index within the job |\n| 4 | machine_id | long | Machine where task runs (can be empty) |\n| 5 | event_type | int | Type of event (see below) |\n| 6 | user | string | Obfuscated user name |\n| 7 | scheduling_class | int | Scheduling class |\n| 8 | priority | int | Task priority (0-11) |\n| 9 | cpu_request | double | CPU cores requested |\n| 10 | memory_request | double | Memory requested (fraction of machine) |\n| 11 | disk_space_request | double | Disk space requested |\n| 12 | different_machines | int | Constraint flag |\n\n## Job Events Schema (8 columns)\n\n| Index | Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | timestamp | long | Event time in microseconds |\n| 1 | missing_info | string | Info about missing data (often empty) |\n| 2 | job_id | long | Job identifier |\n| 3 | event_type | int | Type of event (see below) |\n| 4 | user | string | Obfuscated user name |\n| 5 | scheduling_class | int | Scheduling class |\n| 6 | job_name | string | Obfuscated job name |\n| 7 | logical_job_name | string | Obfuscated logical job name |\n\n## Event Types (shared by both task and job events)\n\n| Value | Name | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | SUBMIT | Job/task submitted |\n| 1 | SCHEDULE | Job/task scheduled on a machine |\n| 2 | EVICT | Evicted from machine |\n| 3 | FAIL | Failed |\n| 4 | FINISH | Completed successfully |\n| 5 | KILL | Killed |\n| 6 | LOST | Lost (communication failure) |\n| 7 | UPDATE_PENDING | Update while pending |\n| 8 | UPDATE_RUNNING | Update while running |\n\n## Data Characteristics\n- Fields can be empty (e.g., machine_id when task hasn't been scheduled)\n- CSV has no header row\n- Files are gzip-compressed\n- Job IDs are shared between task_events and job_events tables\n- A task is uniquely identified by (job_id, task_index)\n- The same task may be submitted, evicted/failed, and resubmitted multiple times\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cfc0cf92-9da0-4229-9eba-efcd5d94bf5c"}
{"parentUuid":"20d5607c-42de-491b-b394-3019284bf0a0","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"5d3cc83e-4643-4c1b-a0f8-8286c23c1c00","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"swift-chasing-cookie","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01UZJEyLTS55jbhi45tYgdkc","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-session-window-pattern.md"}]},"uuid":"f9b59ace-9599-4f1b-b9c0-9c961bccce33","timestamp":"2026-02-07T05:48:31.706Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-session-window-pattern.md","content":"# Flink Session Window Pattern for Activity Stages\n\n## Problem\nIdentify \"stages\" of activity for a given key, where a stage is a burst of events separated by inactivity gaps. Then find the stage with the most events.\n\n## Approach: Event-Time Session Windows\n\n### Key Concept\nA session window groups events that occur within a specified gap duration. When no new events arrive for the gap period, the window closes.\n\n### Implementation Pattern\n\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.assigners.EventTimeSessionWindows;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.time.Time;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.windows.TimeWindow;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.functions.windowing.WindowFunction;\nimport org.apache.flink.util.Collector;\n\n// 1. Filter to relevant events (e.g., SUBMIT events only)\nDataStream<TaskEvent> submits = taskEvents.filter(e -> e.getEventType() == 0);\n\n// 2. Assign watermarks based on event time\nDataStream<TaskEvent> withWatermarks = submits\n    .assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(\n        WatermarkStrategy.<TaskEvent>forMonotonousTimestamps()\n            .withTimestampAssigner((event, ts) -> event.getTimestampMs())\n    );\n\n// 3. Key by job ID and apply session window\nDataStream<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> sessionCounts = withWatermarks\n    .keyBy(TaskEvent::getJobId)\n    .window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n    .apply(new WindowFunction<TaskEvent, Tuple2<Long, Integer>, Long, TimeWindow>() {\n        @Override\n        public void apply(Long jobId, TimeWindow window,\n                         Iterable<TaskEvent> input,\n                         Collector<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> out) {\n            int count = 0;\n            for (TaskEvent e : input) {\n                count++;\n            }\n            out.collect(new Tuple2<>(jobId, count));\n        }\n    });\n```\n\n### Finding the Maximum Per Key\nAfter session windows produce counts, find the max per job:\n\n```java\n// Key by jobId again and reduce to find max count\nDataStream<Tuple2<Long, Integer>> maxPerJob = sessionCounts\n    .keyBy(t -> t.f0)\n    .reduce((a, b) -> new Tuple2<>(a.f0, Math.max(a.f1, b.f1)));\n```\n\n**Important**: The `reduce` on a keyed stream is incremental - it keeps the running result and emits on every new element. This means intermediate results are emitted. To get only the final result, either:\n1. Use a `ProcessFunction` with timers\n2. Use the result after all data is processed (works for bounded/batch-like streams)\n3. Use `.maxBy()` in a global window with trigger\n\n### Alternative: Process with CoProcessFunction\nWhen you need to combine task events with job events (e.g., only output when a job finishes):\n\n```java\ntaskStream.connect(jobStream)\n    .keyBy(task -> task.getJobId(), job -> job.getJobId())\n    .process(new CoProcessFunction<TaskSessionResult, JobEvent, Output>() {\n        // Use ValueState to track max session count\n        // Use ListState to buffer results until job finishes\n    });\n```\n\n## Output Format\nFor `Tuple2<Long, Integer>`, Flink's `toString()` produces: `(value1,value2)`\nUsing `.writeAsText()` will write one tuple per line.\n\n## Parallelism for Single Output File\n```java\nstream.writeAsText(outputPath, FileSystem.WriteMode.OVERWRITE)\n      .setParallelism(1);\n```\n\n## Bounded Stream Considerations\nWhen processing a finite dataset (file source), Flink processes all records then closes windows. The `forMonotonousTimestamps()` watermark strategy works well for sorted data. For out-of-order data, use `forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration)`.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"20d5607c-42de-491b-b394-3019284bf0a0"}
